# Trivy CVE ignores — each entry MUST carry a justification and a re-evaluation
# trigger. This gate fails on fixable HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs (ci.yml: image CVE scan);
# an ignore here is a deliberate, scoped exception, not a blanket suppression.

# CVE-2025-26646 — MSBuild (Microsoft.Build.Tasks.Core) spoofing vulnerability from the
# .NET SDK used by the `csharp` language (G15). This is now a RESIDUAL safety net: the
# Dockerfile SLIMS the SDK to only the NETCore.App runtime + ref pack + Roslyn/bincore
# (csc), DROPPING MSBuild/NuGet/dotnet-format/AspNetCore entirely — so this component
# (and the CVEs in the other dropped tooling: CVE-2025-55247, CVE-2026-26171,
# CVE-2026-33116) is no longer in the image at all. The runner never invokes MSBuild
# regardless (csc-direct, no `dotnet build`/restore, empty netns). Kept only in case a
# Roslyn deps.json transitively re-references it; drop when the csharp SDK is bumped.
CVE-2025-26646
